                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1de6487e-ad11-3c7d-a167-866e5c09272c",
                        "entry_id": "92f9c7a7-1eca-3467-994f-dbe4cf7ad398",
                        "glosses": [
                            "nicht-nasaler, sonorantischer, konsonantischer Dauerlaut; Oberbegriff für Laterale und Vibranten"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d476634-2f14-445f-a8f5-9330f7f7d451",
                                "sense_id": "1de6487e-ad11-3c7d-a167-866e5c09272c",
                                "text": "[l] und [ʀ] sind Liquide im Deutschen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8c0d71f-daee-44a3-b9fd-01d68228031d",
                                "sense_id": "1de6487e-ad11-3c7d-a167-866e5c09272c",
                                "text": "„Die beiden erstgenannten Gruppen beinhalten Doppelkonsonanz mit einem Liquid in zweiter Position, bei denen die Verbindungen mit /l/ weniger häufig fehlrealisiert werden als diejenigen mit /r/.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "67091ad7-9eb9-4683-8329-728405df4cc9",
                        "source_entry_id": "92f9c7a7-1eca-3467-994f-dbe4cf7ad398",
                        "source_sense_id": "1de6487e-ad11-3c7d-a167-866e5c09272c",
                        "target_lang_word": "liquid",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "liquid",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8f26804c-3906-387a-9a2f-fb5db06e1901",
                                        "entry_id": "d2d24f63-c746-36ba-9e99-74f6b497cc89",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A substance that is flowing, and keeping no shape, such as water; a substance of which the molecules, while not tending to separate from one another like those of a gas, readily change their relative position, and which therefore retains no definite shape, except that determined by the containing receptacle; an inelastic fluid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "physical",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08028441-add7-4104-ba8e-cb24c6791776",
                                                "sense_id": "8f26804c-3906-387a-9a2f-fb5db06e1901",
                                                "text": "A liquid can freeze to become a solid or evaporate into a gas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6854cbe2-0a02-45f6-abe0-0fe737cdfc4f",
                                                "sense_id": "8f26804c-3906-387a-9a2f-fb5db06e1901",
                                                "text": "The dawn of the oil age was fairly recent. Although the stuff was used to waterproof boats in the Middle East 6,000 years ago, extracting it in earnest began only in 1859 after an oil strike in Pennsylvania.[…]It was used to make kerosene, the main fuel for artificial lighting after overfishing led to a shortage of whale blubber. Other liquids produced in the refining process, too unstable or smoky for lamplight, were burned or dumped."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c4b6ed4d-1df5-36d8-85dc-a3e83c6a19f1",
                                        "entry_id": "d2d24f63-c746-36ba-9e99-74f6b497cc89",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of a class of consonant sounds that includes l and r."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3a449d1-b9f8-43bd-97f6-1f671bd29d2a",
                                                "sense_id": "c4b6ed4d-1df5-36d8-85dc-a3e83c6a19f1",
                                                "text": "Many female forenames are regarded as euphonyms. What is and is not euphonious is necessarily subjective, but it could be suggested that names containing labials (b, m), sibilants (s, sh) and liquids (l, r) are more likely to be euphonyms than those that do not."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bc57c5c-a588-4718-8a20-93e12b7b500a",
                                                "sense_id": "c4b6ed4d-1df5-36d8-85dc-a3e83c6a19f1",
                                                "text": "[…]-able does not attach to verbs ending in a postconsonantal liquid […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "liquid",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6030e4bc-cd5e-3836-b1d1-42a0369c3541",
                                        "entry_id": "2fa52f4d-a5b5-3f40-a4f8-afddb8bfa80b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Flowing freely like water; fluid; not solid and not gaseous; composed of particles that move freely among each other on the slightest pressure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0988688-4fc2-4675-9d9f-c0c4dbc6cc90",
                                                "sense_id": "6030e4bc-cd5e-3836-b1d1-42a0369c3541",
                                                "text": "liquid nitrogen"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0afd1cd0-d97a-3291-8eb4-5a85082a5af4",
                                        "entry_id": "2fa52f4d-a5b5-3f40-a4f8-afddb8bfa80b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Easily sold or disposed of without losing value."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of an asset"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "59d39ae2-71b7-3a89-89ee-3d67d623994a",
                                        "entry_id": "2fa52f4d-a5b5-3f40-a4f8-afddb8bfa80b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having sufficient trading activity to make buying or selling easy."
                                        ],
